[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186198273 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" "question-025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" :question/id #uuid "e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-181780" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={R}^{+}\\times Z$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={R}^{+}\\times Z\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate is an integer number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+},\\,y\\in Z\\}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+}\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/50/50228bcff5b3678518379cda03257ac234e8312cd23f9b38fa897188c8c5c1c5.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/75/75f8be8dd49241503b705c78e4018a98fead197191b38f856d7fbce069a63de2.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{+}\\times Z & =…{S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${R}^{+}\\times Z$ as the set of horizontal lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/20/2086bcf65608ff2c031da9f6882272fd6d8eb828f3d904c4f0fc946b5fbe108c.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/id #uuid "279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763" :answer-field/choices ["answer-38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763" "answer-23d1723d-bafd-5e2d-8f64-068977702f1d" "answer-0f84b057-93cf-5d03-ad21-48cde768543f" "answer-01577e1c-b63e-57f0-b602-f5ed9e7c099b" "answer-1fc3fdb8-5fd0-510e-90c2-ef266178bfdc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763" :answer/id #uuid "38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/20/2086bcf65608ff2c031da9f6882272fd6d8eb828f3d904c4f0fc946b5fbe108c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23d1723d-bafd-5e2d-8f64-068977702f1d" :answer/id #uuid "23d1723d-bafd-5e2d-8f64-068977702f1d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/4a/4aee0f1bf6bfc1f54a5255fdadd9049bfb44f712d34ee61491bec32d1cb6b42e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f84b057-93cf-5d03-ad21-48cde768543f" :answer/id #uuid "0f84b057-93cf-5d03-ad21-48cde768543f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/89/89ac9e71d8152097657f0c01daecf2b894dc142db4ba27fbfadcb8ded6e9cb19.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01577e1c-b63e-57f0-b602-f5ed9e7c099b" :answer/id #uuid "01577e1c-b63e-57f0-b602-f5ed9e7c099b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/8e/8e2511ab8e06ba3d994e4a5ad13c53867d47265d1407a3a4995ee477a83eb471.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fc3fdb8-5fd0-510e-90c2-ef266178bfdc" :answer/id #uuid "1fc3fdb8-5fd0-510e-90c2-ef266178bfdc" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d3/d3b71b596aef1bc509c1501c0b8020890f0801a37a61116a8733593a7d2780d4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287775 :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=[0,2]\\times \\{-1,0,1\\}$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=[0,2]\\times \\{-1,0,1\\}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is either $-1,0,$ or $1.$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2],\\,y\\in \\{-1,0,1\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]\\}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de9bd6dc79cabf8230b0cec26233958aa0fbb001875b9942cbb7f4d36e6b08fb.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $0.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(x,0)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/81/819c31e4d29dbd3e18c7dea8df495a565d2ede866ec019c764704d6dc47f5c70.png)\n\nNow, consider ${S}_{3}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{3}=\\{(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f335df98dc9cb33ccc96f87d24efa3bd78a4d4c271d0fbaf7ae5e8c30916d9e.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the three line segments shown below.\n\n![](images/a1/a1a9065f9dbb6648100bc6a22bff367916c241dc2eba5f3878d6cf1b9821d4e8.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" :question/id #uuid "025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-181972" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is an integer number and whose $y$-coordinate is a negative integer or zero..\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in Z,\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is negative integer or zero.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/a5/a5d50bdd40efb18b4d29f3e108576e3befcc0d3f3e5b54a0686aeef6e9ffa212.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any negative integer or zero.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/12/129cb0ae2a59415a90118030461244ab7f1faa91aba47b5e0e2864323dbfede9.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/25/25bd7ebe8087af06fa21e4d5f9878d0e5867630372138bad1af241c1ee270d30.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab" "answer-0dbee5dc-e5a6-52c6-8ec3-191a184237ef" "answer-c0815e68-d37c-5b08-9b24-7ed04211e59e" "answer-d3d84521-ef3e-5c0c-b7b9-6d3a3526d965" "answer-cf2c4ec1-bc76-5b71-8506-5c91d013652b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab" :answer/id #uuid "9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/25/25bd7ebe8087af06fa21e4d5f9878d0e5867630372138bad1af241c1ee270d30.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0dbee5dc-e5a6-52c6-8ec3-191a184237ef" :answer/id #uuid "0dbee5dc-e5a6-52c6-8ec3-191a184237ef" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/25/25c6e0dbdeeec44456e198ed668cf23be3f64f97ecdbf8ab172412d689066bba.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0815e68-d37c-5b08-9b24-7ed04211e59e" :answer/id #uuid "c0815e68-d37c-5b08-9b24-7ed04211e59e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/2d/2df87b90d770a5f2c0ba40a55330409d1cd80866b7e34299eab6dcbf675c6a13.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3d84521-ef3e-5c0c-b7b9-6d3a3526d965" :answer/id #uuid "d3d84521-ef3e-5c0c-b7b9-6d3a3526d965" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/32/32c33c9eb7df58d8550a00a1318f6d56e0755916ffeedafd71e13d93431e4911.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf2c4ec1-bc76-5b71-8506-5c91d013652b" :answer/id #uuid "cf2c4ec1-bc76-5b71-8506-5c91d013652b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/80/80c13426f812f1e98b0ffd61d81eeb7c70a04c5013625d6e6d2add5f2d4a6d85.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198274 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a" :question/id #uuid "151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a" :question/math-academy-id "q-184529" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[i,1]\\times \\{i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0.5,1]\\times \\{0.5\\}=\\{(k,0.5)\\,:\\,k\\in [0.5,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0.5,0.5)$ to the point $(1,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/bb/bb8f515fb5c342ece5727830e95bcc617c03a5bf6542f959ba9e020d22f7faef.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[i,1]\\times \\{i\\}=\\{(k,i)\\,:\\,k\\in [i,1]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(i,i)$ to the point $(1,i).$ \n\n![](images/f2/f255d7dede080e93cb135c1087a0f14591467439d891187062a4fa185a8858cf.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/d8/d823dd4dcd675b07b004cf2850059600e861c8b3d259f884d25c61e43431de35.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02a5f76b-f604-59fe-97b6-05e2a5373e9f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02a5f76b-f604-59fe-97b6-05e2a5373e9f" :answer-field/id #uuid "02a5f76b-f604-59fe-97b6-05e2a5373e9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-46294241-6d76-5660-8308-b704b82c7087" :answer-field/choices ["answer-21d1343b-7100-58e3-bed7-c7d90bf7a16a" "answer-d37321c7-1ae7-5d15-94e2-6426d7989dee" "answer-200ed653-8d22-5eba-808d-7a37690a4d53" "answer-579c7f1d-d6a9-5e5b-bcc9-c804ba1b38f0" "answer-46294241-6d76-5660-8308-b704b82c7087"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21d1343b-7100-58e3-bed7-c7d90bf7a16a" :answer/id #uuid "21d1343b-7100-58e3-bed7-c7d90bf7a16a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/17/17aa625cfbc90322745b214bca0c4857885d4338e3628e25074668c832cf0732.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d37321c7-1ae7-5d15-94e2-6426d7989dee" :answer/id #uuid "d37321c7-1ae7-5d15-94e2-6426d7989dee" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/78/78347152f7962f733ea97e43a799f3f1c8318a4ac18608125d26dbd318f664bd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-200ed653-8d22-5eba-808d-7a37690a4d53" :answer/id #uuid "200ed653-8d22-5eba-808d-7a37690a4d53" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/81/8108b38989765e84ab83817d82352bf1d18249a0c7c5d19bc940480564f91d5d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-579c7f1d-d6a9-5e5b-bcc9-c804ba1b38f0" :answer/id #uuid "579c7f1d-d6a9-5e5b-bcc9-c804ba1b38f0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/93/93cc14e996746f6516b412eeb4c71f8df7439bf7d210e36a6b67412feec08225.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46294241-6d76-5660-8308-b704b82c7087" :answer/id #uuid "46294241-6d76-5660-8308-b704b82c7087" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d8/d823dd4dcd675b07b004cf2850059600e861c8b3d259f884d25c61e43431de35.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b6e9d445-0ba2-5cbc-973a-1de35aa7f2c5" :activity/id #uuid "b6e9d445-0ba2-5cbc-973a-1de35aa7f2c5" :activity/title "Visualizing Cartesian Products" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048206 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-8b7cd465-a531-5b2c-aa31-225a1dbba8b6" "step-40115689-6ef7-5297-b4cc-659f1af4234d" "step-929b7ead-827c-5b82-82c3-38ca98ce721d" "step-9b20313e-470b-5bfd-bcdb-18795605d3de" "step-25a9e4f2-d080-581c-9f8c-5e235244e694"] :activity/first-step "step-8b7cd465-a531-5b2c-aa31-225a1dbba8b6" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-8b7cd465-a531-5b2c-aa31-225a1dbba8b6" :step/id #uuid "8b7cd465-a531-5b2c-aa31-225a1dbba8b6" :step/content 17592186198717 :step/next "step-40115689-6ef7-5297-b4cc-659f1af4234d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-40115689-6ef7-5297-b4cc-659f1af4234d" :step/id #uuid "40115689-6ef7-5297-b4cc-659f1af4234d" :step/content "question-e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" :step/next "step-929b7ead-827c-5b82-82c3-38ca98ce721d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-929b7ead-827c-5b82-82c3-38ca98ce721d" :step/id #uuid "929b7ead-827c-5b82-82c3-38ca98ce721d" :step/content 17592186287775 :step/next "step-9b20313e-470b-5bfd-bcdb-18795605d3de" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9b20313e-470b-5bfd-bcdb-18795605d3de" :step/id #uuid "9b20313e-470b-5bfd-bcdb-18795605d3de" :step/content "question-025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" :step/next "step-25a9e4f2-d080-581c-9f8c-5e235244e694" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-25a9e4f2-d080-581c-9f8c-5e235244e694" :step/id #uuid "25a9e4f2-d080-581c-9f8c-5e235244e694" :step/content "question-151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" :question/id #uuid "e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3"] ["question-e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-181780"] ["question-e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={R}^{+}\\times Z$ in the Cartesian plane?"] ["question-e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={R}^{+}\\times Z\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate is an integer number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+},\\,y\\in Z\\}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+}\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/50/50228bcff5b3678518379cda03257ac234e8312cd23f9b38fa897188c8c5c1c5.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/75/75f8be8dd49241503b705c78e4018a98fead197191b38f856d7fbce069a63de2.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{+}\\times Z & =…{S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${R}^{+}\\times Z$ as the set of horizontal lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/20/2086bcf65608ff2c031da9f6882272fd6d8eb828f3d904c4f0fc946b5fbe108c.png)"] ["question-e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/id #uuid "279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617"] ["answer-38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763" :answer/id #uuid "38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763"] ["answer-38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763" :answer/value "images/20/2086bcf65608ff2c031da9f6882272fd6d8eb828f3d904c4f0fc946b5fbe108c.png"] ["answer-23d1723d-bafd-5e2d-8f64-068977702f1d" :answer/id #uuid "23d1723d-bafd-5e2d-8f64-068977702f1d"] ["answer-23d1723d-bafd-5e2d-8f64-068977702f1d" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-23d1723d-bafd-5e2d-8f64-068977702f1d" :answer/value "images/4a/4aee0f1bf6bfc1f54a5255fdadd9049bfb44f712d34ee61491bec32d1cb6b42e.png"] ["answer-0f84b057-93cf-5d03-ad21-48cde768543f" :answer/id #uuid "0f84b057-93cf-5d03-ad21-48cde768543f"] ["answer-0f84b057-93cf-5d03-ad21-48cde768543f" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-0f84b057-93cf-5d03-ad21-48cde768543f" :answer/value "images/89/89ac9e71d8152097657f0c01daecf2b894dc142db4ba27fbfadcb8ded6e9cb19.png"] ["answer-01577e1c-b63e-57f0-b602-f5ed9e7c099b" :answer/id #uuid "01577e1c-b63e-57f0-b602-f5ed9e7c099b"] ["answer-01577e1c-b63e-57f0-b602-f5ed9e7c099b" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-01577e1c-b63e-57f0-b602-f5ed9e7c099b" :answer/value "images/8e/8e2511ab8e06ba3d994e4a5ad13c53867d47265d1407a3a4995ee477a83eb471.png"] ["answer-1fc3fdb8-5fd0-510e-90c2-ef266178bfdc" :answer/id #uuid "1fc3fdb8-5fd0-510e-90c2-ef266178bfdc"] ["answer-1fc3fdb8-5fd0-510e-90c2-ef266178bfdc" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-1fc3fdb8-5fd0-510e-90c2-ef266178bfdc" :answer/value "images/d3/d3b71b596aef1bc509c1501c0b8020890f0801a37a61116a8733593a7d2780d4.png"] ["answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/correct "answer-38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763"] ["answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/choices "answer-38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763"] ["answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/choices "answer-23d1723d-bafd-5e2d-8f64-068977702f1d"] ["answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/choices "answer-0f84b057-93cf-5d03-ad21-48cde768543f"] ["answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/choices "answer-01577e1c-b63e-57f0-b602-f5ed9e7c099b"] ["answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/choices "answer-1fc3fdb8-5fd0-510e-90c2-ef266178bfdc"] ["question-e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617"] [17592186198273 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3"] [17592186287775 :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=[0,2]\\times \\{-1,0,1\\}$ in the Cartesian plane?"] [17592186287775 :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=[0,2]\\times \\{-1,0,1\\}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is either $-1,0,$ or $1.$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2],\\,y\\in \\{-1,0,1\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]\\}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de9bd6dc79cabf8230b0cec26233958aa0fbb001875b9942cbb7f4d36e6b08fb.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $0.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(x,0)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/81/819c31e4d29dbd3e18c7dea8df495a565d2ede866ec019c764704d6dc47f5c70.png)\n\nNow, consider ${S}_{3}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{3}=\\{(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f335df98dc9cb33ccc96f87d24efa3bd78a4d4c271d0fbaf7ae5e8c30916d9e.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the three line segments shown below.\n\n![](images/a1/a1a9065f9dbb6648100bc6a22bff367916c241dc2eba5f3878d6cf1b9821d4e8.png)"] ["question-025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" :question/id #uuid "025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc"] ["question-025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-181972"] ["question-025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}$ in the Cartesian plane?"] ["question-025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is an integer number and whose $y$-coordinate is a negative integer or zero..\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in Z,\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is negative integer or zero.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/a5/a5d50bdd40efb18b4d29f3e108576e3befcc0d3f3e5b54a0686aeef6e9ffa212.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any negative integer or zero.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/12/129cb0ae2a59415a90118030461244ab7f1faa91aba47b5e0e2864323dbfede9.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/25/25bd7ebe8087af06fa21e4d5f9878d0e5867630372138bad1af241c1ee270d30.png)"] ["question-025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65"] ["answer-9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab" :answer/id #uuid "9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab"] ["answer-9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab" :answer/value "images/25/25bd7ebe8087af06fa21e4d5f9878d0e5867630372138bad1af241c1ee270d30.png"] ["answer-0dbee5dc-e5a6-52c6-8ec3-191a184237ef" :answer/id #uuid "0dbee5dc-e5a6-52c6-8ec3-191a184237ef"] ["answer-0dbee5dc-e5a6-52c6-8ec3-191a184237ef" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-0dbee5dc-e5a6-52c6-8ec3-191a184237ef" :answer/value "images/25/25c6e0dbdeeec44456e198ed668cf23be3f64f97ecdbf8ab172412d689066bba.png"] ["answer-c0815e68-d37c-5b08-9b24-7ed04211e59e" :answer/id #uuid "c0815e68-d37c-5b08-9b24-7ed04211e59e"] ["answer-c0815e68-d37c-5b08-9b24-7ed04211e59e" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-c0815e68-d37c-5b08-9b24-7ed04211e59e" :answer/value "images/2d/2df87b90d770a5f2c0ba40a55330409d1cd80866b7e34299eab6dcbf675c6a13.png"] ["answer-d3d84521-ef3e-5c0c-b7b9-6d3a3526d965" :answer/id #uuid "d3d84521-ef3e-5c0c-b7b9-6d3a3526d965"] ["answer-d3d84521-ef3e-5c0c-b7b9-6d3a3526d965" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-d3d84521-ef3e-5c0c-b7b9-6d3a3526d965" :answer/value "images/32/32c33c9eb7df58d8550a00a1318f6d56e0755916ffeedafd71e13d93431e4911.png"] ["answer-cf2c4ec1-bc76-5b71-8506-5c91d013652b" :answer/id #uuid "cf2c4ec1-bc76-5b71-8506-5c91d013652b"] ["answer-cf2c4ec1-bc76-5b71-8506-5c91d013652b" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-cf2c4ec1-bc76-5b71-8506-5c91d013652b" :answer/value "images/80/80c13426f812f1e98b0ffd61d81eeb7c70a04c5013625d6e6d2add5f2d4a6d85.png"] ["answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/correct "answer-9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab"] ["answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/choices "answer-9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab"] ["answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/choices "answer-0dbee5dc-e5a6-52c6-8ec3-191a184237ef"] ["answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/choices "answer-c0815e68-d37c-5b08-9b24-7ed04211e59e"] ["answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/choices "answer-d3d84521-ef3e-5c0c-b7b9-6d3a3526d965"] ["answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/choices "answer-cf2c4ec1-bc76-5b71-8506-5c91d013652b"] ["question-025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65"] [17592186198273 :knowledge-point/questions "question-025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc"] ["question-151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a" :question/id #uuid "151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a"] ["question-151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a" :question/math-academy-id "q-184529"] ["question-151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[i,1]\\times \\{i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$"] ["question-151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0.5,1]\\times \\{0.5\\}=\\{(k,0.5)\\,:\\,k\\in [0.5,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0.5,0.5)$ to the point $(1,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/bb/bb8f515fb5c342ece5727830e95bcc617c03a5bf6542f959ba9e020d22f7faef.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[i,1]\\times \\{i\\}=\\{(k,i)\\,:\\,k\\in [i,1]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(i,i)$ to the point $(1,i).$ \n\n![](images/f2/f255d7dede080e93cb135c1087a0f14591467439d891187062a4fa185a8858cf.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/d8/d823dd4dcd675b07b004cf2850059600e861c8b3d259f884d25c61e43431de35.png)"] ["question-151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-02a5f76b-f604-59fe-97b6-05e2a5373e9f" :answer-field/id #uuid "02a5f76b-f604-59fe-97b6-05e2a5373e9f"] ["answer-21d1343b-7100-58e3-bed7-c7d90bf7a16a" :answer/id #uuid "21d1343b-7100-58e3-bed7-c7d90bf7a16a"] ["answer-21d1343b-7100-58e3-bed7-c7d90bf7a16a" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-21d1343b-7100-58e3-bed7-c7d90bf7a16a" :answer/value "images/17/17aa625cfbc90322745b214bca0c4857885d4338e3628e25074668c832cf0732.png"] ["answer-d37321c7-1ae7-5d15-94e2-6426d7989dee" :answer/id #uuid "d37321c7-1ae7-5d15-94e2-6426d7989dee"] ["answer-d37321c7-1ae7-5d15-94e2-6426d79